🗳️ ONLINE VOTING SYSTEM – PROJECT REPORT

 1. Introduction:

An Online Voting System is a web-based application that allows users to vote securely from anywhere. It replaces traditional paper voting and ensures accuracy, transparency, and efficiency.

2. Objectives:

To create a secure digital voting platform
To reduce manual errors in elections
To provide fast and reliable results
To ensure one person can vote only once.

3. Features:

User Registration & Login
Admin Panel for managing elections
Candidate List Display
Secure Voting System
Real-time Vote Counting
Result Declaration

4. Technologies Used:

Frontend:
HTML
CSS
JavaScript

Backend:
Node.js / Express.js (or Python Flask if you prefer)

Database:
MySQL (or MongoDB)

5. System Architecture:

User interacts through browser
Frontend sends request to backend server
Backend processes data
Database stores users, votes, candidates.

6. Database Design:

Users Table
user_id
name
email
password
has_voted
Candidates Table
candidate_id
name
party
Votes Table
vote_id
user_id
candidate_id

7.How It Works:

User registers and logs in
Admin adds candidates
User selects a candidate
Vote is recorded in database
User cannot vote again
Results are calculated automatically.

8.Security Features:

Authentication system
One vote per user restriction
Data stored securely in database

9.Future Enhancements:

OTP / Aadhaar-based authentication
Blockchain-based voting
Mobile app integration
Advanced admin dashboard.

10.Advantages:

Fast and accurate voting
Saves time and paper
Easy to use interface
Accessible from anywhere.

11.Limitations:

Requires internet connection
Basic security (can be improved).


